// A hardware watchdog (component E13): what its driver provides.

/// A watchdog: a timer in the machine that resets it unless it is petted
/// before the timer runs out. It runs from the moment its driver starts.
///
/// The service manager is its only client (the device manager gives a
/// capability to it to nobody else): it pets the watchdog from its own
/// loop, so the machine is reset when the service manager or the kernel
/// stops making progress, and nothing else can keep a hung machine alive
/// by petting for it. A machine without a watchdog has no driver for one,
/// and the service manager says so at boot.
protocol silica.watchdog.Device version 1 {
    /// How long the watchdog waits for a pet before it resets the
    /// machine, and whether it reset the machine last time (the reason
    /// this boot happened).
    info @1 () -> (timeout_ms: u32, reset_last_boot: bool);

    /// Start the timer over.
    pet @2 () -> ();
}
